  "digitizer_notes": "Color NEGATIVE film (not reversal) -- curves increasing with exposure, identity via clear inline rotated labels (Blue/Green/Red) directly on each curve, no ambiguity: Blue highest, Green middle, Red lowest, confirmed both visually and by toe density order. Gridline removal uses morphological opening (binary_opening with a 1x61 horizontal and 61x1 vertical structuring element) instead of a fixed global row/column list -- confirmed (2026-07-06, user-suggested direction) that this chart's gridlines are very slightly TILTED (drift a few px in row position across the image width), so a single fixed-width deletion band either over-deletes or under-deletes depending on where it's calibrated from. Morphological opening adapts to the gridline's true local position/thickness at every point. Structuring-element size 61 (41 left a false gridline-value artifact from label sub-strokes; 101 reintroduced a different violation). x_range starts at image-col 165 (~exposure -3.54), matching where the real plotted curves start -- confirmed the frame extends to -4.0 but Fuji's own plotted data doesn't. QA overlay: both a combined (all 3 curves) plot and one PNG per curve, so a curve's fit through the merged/converged region is directly checkable without other curves' dots obscuring it."
